# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# AICHIEVE/ is a SEPARATE repository (kotechile/achieve → aichieve.net).
# It lives here only as a working directory during the 2026 split. Its own git
# history, node_modules and build output must never be committed into giniloh.com.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
AICHIEVE/

# Generated at image build time from src/data/ownership.mjs by
# scripts/generate-nginx-redirects.mjs. Never hand-edit; regenerate with `npm run redirects`.
nginx-redirects.conf

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `brag` skill output. Rendered media (brag.mp4, brag.jpg) plus its composition
# and copy drafts — ~12.6MB per run, and a new timestamped directory each time.
# Generated artifacts, not source. Media in git is permanent: once committed it
# is in every clone forever, so these stay out of history entirely.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
brag-output*/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# O*NET 31.0 inputs. task_statements / task_ratings / tasks_to_dwas / work_activities
# are committed: they drive the published scores. work_context.csv is 51 MB and is used
# only to validate the index, so it is fetched on demand instead.
#   bash scripts/onet/fetch_onet.sh
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
data/onet/work_context.csv
